  "modelName": "Qwen3-Coder-Next-GGUF",
  "prompt": "You are an expert JavaScript developer. Create a single-page, standalone HTML document containing a fully playable \"Tango\" logic puzzle game.\n\nSTRICT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n1. ALL HTML, CSS, and JavaScript must be contained within a single file. No external libraries.\n2. Do NOT output markdown code blocks (```html). Start exactly with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>.\n\nTHEME & VISUALS:\n1. The game must look polished and modern, utilizing a clean, balanced interface.\n2. The grid must be 6x6 cells.\n3. The two playing symbols MUST be the Fire emoji (\ud83d\udd25) and the Ice Cube emoji (\ud83e\uddca).\n4. Constraint markers must clearly sit on the borders between adjacent cells using an Equals sign (=) or a Cross (\u00d7).\n\nCORE GAMEPLAY RULES:\n1. Row and Column Balance: Every row and every column must contain exactly three \ud83d\udd25 and three \ud83e\uddca.\n2. No Three in a Row: You cannot place three identical symbols adjacent to each other horizontally or vertically.\n3. Constraint Markers:\n   - '=' (Equals): The two adjacent cells must contain the same symbol.\n   - '\u00d7' (Cross): The two adjacent cells must contain opposite symbols.\n4. Interactivity: Clicking a cell should cycle its state: Empty -> \ud83d\udd25 -> \ud83e\uddca -> Empty.\n\nBACK-END LOGIC & PROCEDURAL GENERATION SPECS:\nThe game MUST generate a brand new, random, playable board on every page load. Implement the generation using this sequence:\n1. Solution Generation (Backtracking): Write a recursive backtracking function to generate a fully populated, valid 6x6 grid that obeys the Balance and No-Three-In-A-Row rules. \n2. Constraint Placement: Once a valid solved board exists, randomly select 6 to 8 pairs of adjacent cells. If the cells share the same symbol, place an '=' marker between them. If they are different, place an '\u00d7' marker.\n3. Puzzle Creation: After placing constraints, randomly clear (empty) 70% of the cells, leaving a few starting symbols and the constraint markers as hints for the player.\n4. Validation: Implement a \"Check Solution\" button that compares the user's current grid against the underlying rules (Balance, No-Three-In-A-Row, and Constraints). Highlight any errors in red.\n\nEnsure the state management clearly separates the \"solution board\" from the \"player board\", and that markers overlay the grid lines cleanly using CSS absolute positioning or a highly refined Grid layout.\n",
  "rawOutput": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Tango Logic Puzzle</title>\n    <style>\n        :root {\n            --bg-color: #f0f2f5;\n            --text-color: #333;\n            --grid-border: #333;\n            --cell-bg: #ffffff;\n            --highlight-color: #e8f0fe;\n            --fire-color: #ff4500;\n            --ice-color: #00bfff;\n            --constraint-color: #555;\n            --error-color: #ff0000;\n            --success-color: #28a745;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n            background-color: var(--bg-color);\n            color: var(--text-color);\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            min-height: 100vh;\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 20px;\n        }\n\n        h1 {\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n            font-weight: 600;\n            letter-spacing: 1px;\n        }\n\n        .instructions {\n            max-width: 600px;\n            text-align: center;\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n            color: #555;\n        }\n\n        .game-container {\n            display: flex;\n            flex-direction: column;\n            align-items: center;\n            gap: 20px;\n        }\n\n        .controls {\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 15px;\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n        }\n\n        button {\n            padding: 10px 20px;\n            font-size: 1rem;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            border: none;\n            border-radius: 5px;\n            background-color: #333;\n            color: white;\n            transition: background-color 0.2s;\n            font-weight: 500;\n        }\n\n        button:hover {\n            background-color: #555;\n        }\n\n        button.secondary {\n            background-color: #6c757d;\n        }\n\n        button.secondary:hover {\n            background-color: #78828d;\n        }\n\n        .status-bar {\n            height: 24px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n\n        .status-bar.error { color: var(--error-color); }\n        .status-bar.success { color: var(--success-color); }\n\n        .puzzle-board {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 360px;\n            height: 360px;\n            background-color: var(--grid-border);\n            border: 2px solid var(--grid-border);\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);\n            grid-template-rows: repeat(6, 1fr);\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\n        }\n\n        .cell {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 60px;\n            height: 60px;\n            background-color: var(--cell-bg);\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            font-size: 2.5rem;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            user-select: none;\n            transition: background-color 0.1s;\n        }\n\n        .cell:hover {\n            background-color: var(--highlight-color);\n        }\n\n        .cell.fixed {\n            background-color: #f8f9fa;\n            cursor: default;\n        }\n\n        .cell.fixed::after {\n            content: '';\n            position: absolute;\n            bottom: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 3px;\n            background-color: #ccc;\n        }\n\n        .cell.error {\n            background-color: #ffe0e0;\n        }\n\n        .constraint {\n            position: absolute;\n            background-color: var(--bg-color);\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: var(--constraint-color);\n            z-index: 10;\n        }\n\n        /* Horizontal Constraints */\n        .constraint-h {\n            width: 60px;\n            height: 4px;\n            top: -2px;\n            left: 0;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n        }\n\n        /* Vertical Constraints */\n        .constraint-v {\n            width: 4px;\n            height: 60px;\n            left: -2px;\n            top: 0;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n        }\n\n        .legend {\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 30px;\n            margin-top: 10px;\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\n        }\n\n        .legend-item {\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            gap: 8px;\n        }\n\n        .legend-icon {\n            font-size: 1.5rem;\n        }\n\n        .legend-symbol {\n            font-weight: bold;\n        }\n\n        .legend-constraint {\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 400px) {\n            .puzzle-board {\n                width: 300px;\n                height: 300px;\n            }\n            .cell {\n                width: 50px;\n                height: 50px;\n                font-size: 2rem;\n            }\n            .constraint-h { width: 50px; }\n            .constraint-v { height: 50px; }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n    <h1>Tango Puzzle</h1>\n    \n    <div class=\"instructions\">\n        <p>Fill the 6\u00d76 grid with Fire (\ud83d\udd25) and Ice (\ud83e\uddca) symbols.</p>\n        <p><strong>Rules:</strong> 1. Each row and column must have exactly 3 of each symbol.<br>\n        2. No three identical symbols in a row (horizontally or vertically).<br>\n        3. Match (=) means adjacent cells are the same. Cross (\u00d7) means they are different.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"game-container\">\n        <div class=\"controls\">\n            <button onclick=\"game.newGame()\">New Game</button>\n            <button class=\"secondary\" onclick=\"game.checkSolution()\">Check Solution</button>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"status-bar\" id=\"statusMessage\"></div>\n\n        <div class=\"puzzle-board\" id=\"board\">\n            <!-- Grid generated by JS -->\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"legend\">\n            <div class=\"legend-item\">\n                <span class=\"legend-icon\">\ud83d\udd25</span>\n                <span class=\"legend-symbol\">Fire</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"legend-item\">\n                <span class=\"legend-icon\">\ud83e\uddca</span>\n                <span class=\"legend-symbol\">Ice</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"legend-item\">\n                <span class=\"legend-constraint\">=</span>\n                <span>Same</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"legend-item\">\n                <span class=\"legend-constraint\">\u00d7</span>\n                <span>Different</span>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        class TangoGame {\n            constructor() {\n                this.boardSize = 6;\n                this.gridElement = document.getElementById('board');\n                this.statusElement = document.getElementById('statusMessage');\n                this.solutionBoard = [];\n                this.playerBoard = [];\n                this.fixedCells = [];\n                this.constraints = [];\n                this.init();\n            }\n\n            init() {\n                this.newGame();\n            }\n\n            newGame() {\n                this.clearStatus();\n                this.solutionBoard = this.generateSolution();\n                this.placeConstraints();\n                this.setupPlayerBoard();\n                this.renderBoard();\n            }\n\n            clearStatus() {\n                this.statusElement.textContent = '';\n                this.statusElement.className = 'status-bar';\n            }\n\n            setStatus(message, type) {\n                this.statusElement.textContent = message;\n                this.statusElement.className = `status-bar ${type}`;\n            }\n\n            // --- Back-End Logic: Solution Generation ---\n\n            generateSolution() {\n                const grid = Array(this.boardSize).fill(null).map(() => Array(this.boardSize).fill(null));\n                this.fillGrid(grid, 0, 0);\n                return grid;\n            }\n\n            fillGrid(grid, row, col) {\n                if (row === this.boardSize) return true; // Done\n\n                const nextRow = col === this.boardSize - 1 ? row + 1 : row;\n                const nextCol = col === this.boardSize - 1 ? 0 : col + 1;\n\n                const symbols = ['\ud83d\udd25', '\ud83e\uddca'];\n                // Shuffle symbols for randomness\n                symbols.sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5);\n\n                for (let symbol of symbols) {\n                    if (this.isValidPlacement(grid, row, col, symbol)) {\n                        grid[row][col] = symbol;\n                        if (this.fillGrid(grid, nextRow, nextCol)) {\n                            return true;\n                        }\n                        grid[row][col] = null; // Backtrack\n                    }\n                }\n                return false;\n            }\n\n            isValidPlacement(grid, row, col, symbol) {\n                // Rule 1: No three in a row\n                // Check horizontal\n                if (col >= 2 && grid[row][col - 1] === symbol && grid[row][col - 2] === symbol) {\n                    return false;\n                }\n                // Check vertical\n                if (row >= 2 && grid[row - 1][col] === symbol && grid[row - 2][col] === symbol) {\n                    return false;\n                }\n\n                // Rule 2: Row/Column Balance (3 of each)\n                // Check row count so far\n                let rowCount = 0;\n                for (let c = 0; c < col; c++) {\n                    if (grid[row][c] === symbol) rowCount++;\n                }\n                // If we add this, can we still fit 3 total? (3 - rowCount - 1 remaining spots in row must be >= 0)\n                // And we need to leave room for the other symbol\n                if (rowCount >= 3) return false; // Already too many of this symbol in row\n\n                // Check column count so far\n                let colCount = 0;\n                for (let r = 0; r < row; r++) {\n                    if (grid[r][col] === symbol) colCount++;\n                }\n                if (colCount >= 3) return false; // Already too many of this symbol in col\n\n                return true;\n            }\n\n            // --- Constraint Placement ---\n\n            placeConstraints() {\n                this.constraints = [];\n                const possiblePairs = [];\n\n                // Collect all adjacent pairs (right and down)\n                for (let r = 0; r < this.boardSize; r++) {\n                    for (let c = 0; c < this.boardSize; c++) {\n                        if (c < this.boardSize - 1) {\n                            possiblePairs.push({ r1: r, c1: c, r2: r, c2: c + 1, type: 'h' });\n                        }\n                        if (r < this.boardSize - 1) {\n                            possiblePairs.push({ r1: r, c1: c, r2: r + 1, c2: c, type: 'v' });\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // Shuffle pairs for randomness\n                possiblePairs.sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5);\n\n                // Select 6 to 8 constraints\n                const numConstraints = Math.floor(Math.random() * 3) + 6; // 6, 7, or 8\n                \n                for (let i = 0; i < numConstraints; i++) {\n                    const pair = possiblePairs[i];\n                    const sym1 = this.solutionBoard[pair.r1][pair.c1];\n                    const sym2 = this.solutionBoard[pair.r2][pair.c2];\n\n                    const constraint = {\n                        r1: pair.r1, c1: pair.c1,\n                        r2: pair.r2, c2: pair.c2,\n                        type: pair.type,\n                        symbol: sym1 === sym2 ? '=' : '\u00d7'\n                    };\n                    this.constraints.push(constraint);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // --- Setup Player Board ---\n\n            setupPlayerBoard() {\n                this.playerBoard = Array(this.boardSize).fill(null).map(() => Array(this.boardSize).fill(null));\n                this.fixedCells = Array(this.boardSize).fill(null).map(() => Array(this.boardSize).fill(false));\n\n                // Randomly clear ~70% of cells\n                for (let r = 0; r < this.boardSize; r++) {\n                    for (let c = 0; c < this.boardSize; c++) {\n                        if (Math.random() > 0.7) {\n                            this.playerBoard[r][c] = null; // Empty\n                            this.fixedCells[r][c] = false;\n                        } else {\n                            this.playerBoard[r][c] = this.solutionBoard[r][c];\n                            this.fixedCells[r][c] = true;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            // --- Rendering ---\n\n            renderBoard() {\n                this.gridElement.innerHTML = '';\n                \n                // Create cells\n                for (let r = 0; r < this.boardSize; r++) {\n                    for (let c = 0; c < this.boardSize; c++) {\n                        const cell = document.createElement('div');\n                        cell.className = 'cell';\n                        cell.dataset.row = r;\n                        cell.dataset.col = c;\n\n                        if (this.fixedCells[r][c]) {\n                            cell.classList.add('fixed');\n                            cell.textContent = this.playerBoard[r][c];\n                        } else {\n                            if (this.playerBoard[r][c]) {\n                                cell.textContent = this.playerBoard[r][c];\n                            }\n                        }\n\n                        cell.addEventListener('click', () => this.handleCellClick(r, c, cell));\n                        this.gridElement.appendChild(cell);\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // Create constraints\n                this.constraints.forEach(constraint => {\n                    const constEl = document.createElement('div');\n                    constEl.className = `constraint ${constraint.type === 'h' ? 'constraint-h' : 'constraint-v'}`;\n                    constEl.textContent = constraint.symbol;\n\n                    // Positioning logic\n                    // Horizontal constraint sits between (r, c) and (r, c+1)\n                    // Vertical constraint sits between (r, c) and (r+1, c)\n                    \n                    // We use CSS absolute positioning relative to the grid container\n                    // Each cell is 60px (or responsive). \n                    // For horizontal: top is row * cellSize, left is (col + 1) * cellSize - half constraint width\n                    // For vertical: top is (row + 1) * cellSize - half constraint height, left is col * cellSize\n                    \n                    // To make it responsive, we use percentages\n                    const cellSizePct = 100 / this.boardSize;\n                    \n                    if (constraint.type === 'h') {\n                        // Between col c and c+1 in row r\n                        // Left: (c + 1) * 16.66% = approx 16.66 * (c+1)\n                        // Width: 16.66%\n                        const leftPos = (constraint.c1 + 1) * cellSizePct;\n                        const topPos = constraint.r1 * cellSizePct;\n                        \n                        constEl.style.left = `${leftPos}%`;\n                        constEl.style.top = `${topPos}%`;\n                        constEl.style.width = `${cellSizePct}%`;\n                        constEl.style.height = '4px'; // Fixed height for visual distinction\n                    } else {\n                        // Between row r and r+1 in col c\n                        const leftPos = constraint.c1 * cellSizePct;\n                        const topPos = (constraint.r1 + 1) * cellSizePct;\n                        \n                        constEl.style.left = `${leftPos}%`;\n                        constEl.style.top = `${topPos}%`;\n                        constEl.style.width = '4px';\n                        constEl.style.height = `${cellSizePct}%`;\n                    }\n\n                    this.gridElement.appendChild(constEl);\n                });\n            }\n\n            // --- Interaction ---\n\n            handleCellClick(r, c, cellElement) {\n                if (this.fixedCells[r][c]) return;\n\n                // Cycle: Empty -> Fire -> Ice -> Empty\n                const current = this.playerBoard[r][c];\n                if (current === null) {\n                    this.playerBoard[r][c] = '\ud83d\udd25';\n                    cellElement.textContent = '\ud83d\udd25';\n                } else if (current === '\ud83d\udd25') {\n                    this.playerBoard[r][c] = '\ud83e\uddca';\n                    cellElement.textContent = '\ud83e\uddca';\n                } else {\n                    this.playerBoard[r][c] = null;\n                    cellElement.textContent = '';\n                }\n                \n                // Clear any error styling on this cell\n                cellElement.classList.remove('error');\n            }\n\n            // --- Validation ---\n\n            checkSolution() {\n                let isCorrect = true;\n                let isComplete = true;\n                let errorsFound = false;\n\n                // 1. Check Completeness\n                for (let r = 0; r < this.boardSize; r++) {\n                    for (let c = 0; c < this.boardSize; c++) {\n                        if (this.playerBoard[r][c] === null) {\n                            isComplete = false;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n                if (!isComplete) {\n                    this.setStatus(\"Board is not complete yet.\", \"error\");\n                    return;\n                }\n\n                // 2. Check Constraints\n                for (let constraint of this.constraints) {\n                    const sym1 = this.playerBoard[constraint.r1][constraint.c1];\n                    const sym2 = this.playerBoard[constraint.r2][constraint.c2];\n                    \n                    let constraintMet = false;\n                    if (constraint.symbol === '=') {\n                        constraintMet = (sym1 === sym2);\n                    } else {\n                        constraintMet = (sym1 !== sym2);\n                    }\n\n                    if (!constraintMet) {\n                        this.markError(constraint.r1, constraint.c1);\n                        this.markError(constraint.r2, constraint.c2);\n                        errorsFound = true;\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // 3. Check Three-in-a-Row\n                for (let r = 0; r < this.boardSize; r++) {\n                    for (let c = 0; c < this.boardSize; c++) {\n                        const current = this.playerBoard[r][c];\n                        if (current === null) continue;\n\n                        // Horizontal\n                        if (c < this.boardSize - 2) {\n                            if (current === this.playerBoard[r][c+1] && current === this.playerBoard[r][c+2]) {\n                                this.markError(r, c);\n                                this.markError(r, c+1);\n                                this.markError(r, c+2);\n                                errorsFound = true;\n                            }\n                        }\n                        // Vertical\n                        if (r < this.boardSize - 2) {\n                            if (current === this.playerBoard[r+1][c] && current === this.playerBoard[r+2][c]) {\n                                this.markError(r, c);\n                                this.markError(r+1, c);\n                                this.markError(r+2, c);\n                                errorsFound = true;\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // 4. Check Balance (3 of each per row/col)\n                // Check Rows\n                for (let r = 0; r < this.boardSize; r++) {\n                    let fireCount = 0;\n                    let iceCount = 0;\n                    for (let c = 0; c < this.boardSize; c++) {\n                        if (this.playerBoard[r][c] === '\ud83d\udd25') fireCount++;\n                        if (this.playerBoard[r][c] === '\ud83e\uddca') iceCount++;\n                    }\n                    if (fireCount !== 3 || iceCount !== 3) {\n                        errorsFound = true;\n                        // Highlight entire row for balance error (optional, but helpful)\n                        // For now, we just flag the logic\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // Check Columns\n                for (let c = 0; c < this.boardSize; c++) {\n                    let fireCount = 0;\n                    let iceCount = 0;\n                    for (let r = 0; r < this.boardSize; r++) {\n                        if (this.playerBoard[r][c] === '\ud83d\udd25') fireCount++;\n                        if (this.playerBoard[r][c] === '\ud83e\uddca') iceCount++;\n                    }\n                    if (fireCount !== 3 || iceCount !== 3) {\n                        errorsFound = true;\n                    }\n                }\n\n                if (errorsFound) {\n                    this.setStatus(\"Errors found! Check the red cells.\", \"error\");\n                } else {\n                    this.setStatus(\"Congratulations! Solution is correct.\", \"success\");\n                }\n            }\n\n            markError(r, c) {\n                // Find the cell in the DOM\n                const cell = this.gridElement.querySelector(`.cell[data-row='${r}'][data-col='${c}']`);\n                if (cell) {\n                    cell.classList.add('error');\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Initialize Game\n        const game = new TangoGame();\n\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
